" :question/math-academy-id "q-136875" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}-8{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=4 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=-3\\end{aligned}\\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}20 & a & 10 \\\\ c & 80 & -20 \\\\ 10 & -20 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}22 \\\\ b \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear equations and its corresponding normal equation shown above. What is the value of $a-b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write our system in matrix form as $Ax=b,$ where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -8 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe normal equation corresponding to $Ax=b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ -8 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & -8 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ -8 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}20 & -40 & 10 \\\\ -40 & 80 & -20 \\\\ 10 & -20 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}22 \\\\ -44 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\na-b+c=(-40)-(-44)+(-40)=-36.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-136875/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fda08f5d-4513-5be0-b8c4-475e82f9bf5a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-136875"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-136811/selection/2671fdc3a44bd3421ded09be4e881743067a96eb4e584e442a30f737593eae71" :answer/id #uuid "c553329f-bced-55e1-908c-cf4cdd179dec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "38" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-1368