ion corresponding to the system $Ax=b$ is given below, what is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & 20 \\\\ 20 & b\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The normal equation corresponding to $Ax=b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -6 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -6 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}10 & 20 \\\\ 20 & 40\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=10+40+(-2)=48.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-136811/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fda08f5d-4513-5be0-b8c4-475e82f9bf5a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-136811"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-136822/selection/283bc09f1a097ae8400558511ca45f1013e17c797fdb7407be52694190fd744b" :answer/id #uuid "85503509-bf55-5fb0-8f88-89056e873bb2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-136822/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" :answer/id #uuid "65f8c321-f324-5f99-ae6e-544d64d5608b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-136822/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "97aee592-b3f2-5ce6-8127-56ca42e08d01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-136822/selection/e0e0a3ac4fe95f021c8f8aece7092270d36ad30c356733db1e628dc4f0b1d434" :answer/id #uuid "4bc3176a-c9ca-5867-91c7-29b0c8c9e31f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-136822/selection/60d8696f019bd6901d4028773e8b64c56a3047a6bc6b4ed12b314cf6b1ae175a" :answer/id #uuid "cb289323-3b53-5217-9813-72c07984b2c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-35" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-136822/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e99c7c9f-200e-5f63-a7d0-c9c8edfc8422" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-136822/selection/e0e0a3ac4fe95f021c8f8aece7092270d36ad30c356733db1e628dc4f0b1d434" :answer-field/choices ["q-136822/selection/283bc09f1a097ae8400558511ca45f1013e17c797fdb7407be52694190fd744b" "q-136822/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" "q-136822/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" "q-136822/selection/e0e0a3ac4fe95f021c8f8aece7092270d36ad30c356733db1e628dc4f0b1d434" "q-136822/selection/60d8696f019bd6901d4028773e8b64c56a3047a6bc6b4ed12b314cf6b1ae175a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-136822" :question/id #uuid "09f1bdf0-428b-503d-8931-22307697fe1f" :question/math-academy-id "q-136822" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}=-2 \\\\ -6{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}+9{x}_{3}=1\\end{aligned}\\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}40 & -20 & -60 \\\\ -20 & 10 & a \\\\ c & 30 & 90\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ b \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear equations and its corresponding normal equation shown above. What is the value of $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write our system in matrix form as $Ax=b,$ where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & -3 \\\\ -6 & 3 & 9\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe normal equation corresponding to $Ax=b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 \\\\ -1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & -3 \\\\ -6 & 3 & 9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 \\\\ -1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}40 & 20 & -60 \\\\ -20 & 10 & 30 \\\\ -60 & 30 & 90\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=30+5+(-60)=-25.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-136822/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fda08f5d-4513-5be0-b8c4-475e82f9bf5a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-136822"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186134298 :question/answer-fields 17592186132230] {:db/id "q-41912/selection/ma-v1/1213c1553989cda6d3005b40cea0cfc88b543c090404d483e9741574c0c7cd3d/801bcdd9cb6a10cec998162e05f71050c8aaf0c6974f095bdcaef715a09f4aee" :answer/id #uuid "0b3303f2-8c1a-5a5d-9904-5e4aeeab52c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "21" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-41912/selection/ma-v1/1213c1553989cda6d3005b40cea0cfc88b543c090404d483e9741574c0c7cd3d/a20b3c9808c291c56ec5bfc5f0f93a856fc692714ca7ebd36c5e4bc361f7075c" :answer/id #uuid "d7ae1f96-0be1-537a-ba9a-ab9ba0a21268" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "42" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-41912/selection/ma-v1/1213c1553989cda6d3005b40cea0cfc88b543c090404d483e9741574c0c7cd3d/cee37ae0a2921bd3973a5cb0592c822dbbfafcfefba8d7007910ead797b9112f" :answer/id #uuid "cae12a7f-986c-5eff-8a42-7a4ed7ba4c1e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "48" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-41912/selection/ma-v1/1213c1553989cda6d3005b40cea0cfc88b543c090404d483e9741574c0c7cd3d/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" :answer/id #uuid "61d4bd6f-7ced-585f-9835-ed2c4a1536c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-41912/selection/ma-v1/1213c1553989cda6d3005b40cea0cfc88b543c090404d483e9741574c0c7cd3d/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" :answer/id #uuid "99d52566-eada-54af-8610-f6b1934d1957" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-41912/selection/ma-v1/1213c1553989cda6d3005b40cea0cfc88b543c090404d483e9741574c0c7cd3d" :answer-field/id #uuid "e7f1636c-f244-53c9-875a-115c6cf53f35" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-41912/selection/ma-v1/1213c1553989cda6d3005b40cea0cfc88b543c090404d483e9741574c0c7cd3d/cee37ae0a2921bd3973a5cb0592c822dbbfafcfefba8d7007910ead797b9112f" :answer-field/choices ["q-41912/selection/ma-v1/1213c1553989cda6d3005b40cea0cfc88b543c090404d483e9741574c0c7cd3d/801bcdd9cb6a10cec998162e05f71050c8aaf0c6974f095bdcaef715a09f4aee" "q-41912/selection/ma-v1/1213c1553989cda6d3005b40cea0cfc88b543c090404d483e9741574c0c7cd3d/a20b3c9808c291c56ec5bfc5f0f93a856fc692714ca7ebd36c5e4bc361f7075c" "q-41912/selection/ma-v1/1213c1553989cda6d3005b40cea0cfc88b543c090404d483e9741574c0c7cd3d/cee37ae0a2921bd3973a5cb0592c822dbbfafcfefba8d7007910ead797b9112f" "q-41912/selection/ma-v1/1213c1553989cda6d3005b40cea0cfc88b543c090404d483e9741574c0c7cd3d/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" "q-41912/selection/ma-v1/1213c1553989cda6d3005b40cea0cfc88b543c090404d483e9741574c0c7cd3d/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-41912"] :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ and vector $b$ above. If the normal equation corresponding to the system $Ax=b$ is given below, what is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & 21 \\\\ 21 & b\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The normal equation corresponding to $Ax=b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}21 & 21 \\\\ 21 & 21\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=21+21+6=48.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-41912/selection/ma-v1/1213c1553989cda6d3005b40cea0cfc88b543c090404d483e9741574c0c7cd3d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-41909"] :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}7{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=5 \\\\ 14{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}245 & 70 & a \\\\ 70 & 20 & 10 \\\\ c & 10 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}35 \\\\ b \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear equations and its corresponding normal equation shown above. What is the value of $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write our system in matrix form as $Ax=b,$ where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 14 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe normal equation corresponding to $Ax=b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}7 & 14 \\\\ 2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 14 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 14 \\\\ 2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}245 & 70 & 35 \\\\ 70 & 20 & 10 \\\\ 35 & 10 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}35 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=35+10+35=80.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-41904/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "093156e5-0a7f-5f70-83e8-6db2dd14ae10" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-41904/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "4710f6eb-ec31-5b96-84c2-8c05baa3b934" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-41904/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "1b632fe9-0e26-5cde-a4c2-ff05071075ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-41904/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "e1987bec-aa0b-5a03-bf0a-603217b752f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-41904/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "17f4d85f-e5be-5639-8dff-430b0bca6149" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-41904/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "53f2c11b-a452-53f6-ac7f-a938d466be03" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-41904/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-41904/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-41904/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-41904/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-41904/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-41904/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-41904" :question/id #uuid "e60c5a85-11ba-5c20-a998-994d66fa6373" :question/math-academy-id "q-41904" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ and vector $b$ shown above. If the general least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R,\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $15a+\\frac{b}{c}?$" :question/worked-solution "The least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the corresponding normal equation:\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}\\,Ax={A}^{T}b\n$$\n\nNotice that the columns of $A$ are linearly dependent. So first, let's write down the normal equation in matrix form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & -4 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & -4 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}40 & -20 \\\\ -20 & 10\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system corresponding to the above matrix equation using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}10 & -5 & 1 \\\\ -10 & 5 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}10 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we have \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\frac{1}{10}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{2}.\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{10}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{10} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n15a+\\frac{b}{c}=15\\cdot \\frac{1}{10}+\\frac{(\\frac{1}{2})}{1}=2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-41904/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9642ac63-6925-5ea3-925d-e697a6222064"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-41904"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-137034/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "4e875a8b-4b2e-5b29-b08b-ed445264c8f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-137034/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "37e602a9-c414-51db-8fca-d21ba1a2a571" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-137034/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "4a528e8f-cecc-53f4-b13a-c4d7eec37ed5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-137034/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "df9f2763-d39d-5223-8e39-4d3092c917cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-137034/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "f2591de9-2046-545c-8f70-b2c8dee86934" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-137034/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c70e5158-2ece-57ae-acb2-c7306756f29a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-137034/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-137034/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-137034/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" "q-137034/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-137034/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-137034/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-137034" :question/id #uuid "a2152687-9e2e-5018-abbd-8ed5e8bc9188" :question/math-academy-id "q-137034" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ and vector $b$ shown above. If the general least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ -\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]\\,+\\,{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ c \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R,\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+2b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "The least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the corresponding normal equation:\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}\\,Ax={A}^{T}b\n$$\n\nThe least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the corresponding normal equation:\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}Ax={A}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nNotice that the columns of $A$ are linearly dependent. So first, let's write down the normal equation in matrix form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system corresponding to the final matrix equation using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 5 & -1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has two pivot columns (the $1$st and $2$nd). Thus, ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable.\n\nFrom the second row, we have \n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-\\frac{1}{5}\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-\\frac{1}{5}-{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nFrom the first row, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=1.\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{5}-{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+2b+c=1+2\\cdot 0+(-1)=0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-137034/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9642ac63-6925-5ea3-925d-e697a6222064"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-137034"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-40943"] :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ and vector $b$ shown above. If the general least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+2b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "The least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the corresponding normal equation:\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}\\,Ax={A}^{T}b\n$$\n\nNotice that the columns of $A$ are linearly dependent. So first, let's write down the normal equation in matrix form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}6 & -8 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 12 & -4 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system corresponding to the final matrix equation using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & -8 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -8 & 12 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -8 & 12 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 6 & -8 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -4 & 6\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has two pivot columns (the $1$st and $2$nd). Thus, ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we have \n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=\\frac{3}{2}+{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n2{x}_{1}-4(\\frac{3}{2}+{x}_{3})+2{x}_{3}=-2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2+{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2+{x}_{3} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}+{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+2b+c=1+2\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}+0=4.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-40950/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "6a235c48-ebd4-5d96-ac78-445ebe1ca8b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40950/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "d9205714-e382-5ab1-8e7f-4434e2b7169a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40950/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "a2c9826a-eadb-561f-80d0-9d2505adba9b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40950/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "7db03a37-c5cb-50be-b600-490746188877" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40950/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "9bbe17dd-7e72-5f62-8dcf-2d00de8661f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40950/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "43770019-6138-5aa7-b875-447631063bc4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-40950/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer-field/choices ["q-40950/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-40950/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-40950/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-40950/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-40950/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-40950" :question/id #uuid "9c15c93a-202f-5422-b992-46722d220d17" :question/math-academy-id "q-40950" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ and vector $b$ shown above. If the general least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}b \\\\ c \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\,+\\,{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R,\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $2a-3b-6c?$" :question/worked-solution "The least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the corresponding normal equation:\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}\\,Ax={A}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nNotice that the columns of $A$ are linearly dependent. So first, let's write down the normal equation in matrix form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}12 & -6 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system corresponding to the above matrix equation using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}12 & -6 & 0 & 12 \\\\ -6 & 3 & 0 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:=2{R}_{2}+{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}12 & -6 & 0 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}↔{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}12 & -6 & 0 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:=(1/6){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{2}:=(1/2){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has two pivot columns (the $1$st and $3$rd). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable.  \n\nFrom the third row, we have\n\n$$\n{x}_{3}=1,\n$$\n\nand from the first row we obtain\n\n$$\n2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=1+\\frac{{x}_{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1+\\frac{{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n2a-3b-6c=2(\\frac{1}{2})-3(1)-6(0)=-2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-40950/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9642ac63-6925-5ea3-925d-e697a6222064"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-40950"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-40921/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "26636dac-94dc-54b3-937a-f5d8b64501fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40921/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "9c6537be-6fbc-5557-bcce-2f147f2f8f83" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40921/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "102334fb-281d-51f1-b08d-10b9377b4e55" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40921/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "e330fe56-a13c-5659-9bdf-799bd795e6c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40921/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "e2c1ca17-575b-58fd-9f9c-452a472af309" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40921/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e854affc-e92d-556a-a578-fede17e66498" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-40921/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-40921/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-40921/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-40921/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-40921/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-40921/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-40921" :question/id #uuid "79003c00-4845-59ab-90de-beecf1933548" :question/math-academy-id "q-40921" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 6 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \n\nConsider the matrix $A$ and vector $b$ shown above. If the general least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ is \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R,\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of  $3a+\\frac{b}{c}?$" :question/worked-solution "The least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the corresponding normal equation:\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}\\,Ax={A}^{T}b\n$$\n\nNotice that the columns of $A$ are linearly dependent. So first, let's write down the normal equation in matrix form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 6 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 6 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 6 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}54 & -18 \\\\ -18 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system corresponding to the above matrix equation using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}54 & -18 & 12 \\\\ -18 & 6 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}54 & -18 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we have \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\frac{2}{9}+\\frac{1}{3}{x}_{2}.\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{9}+\\frac{1}{3}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{9} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n3a+\\frac{b}{c}=3\\cdot \\frac{2}{9}+\\frac{(\\frac{1}{3})}{1}=1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-40921/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9642ac63-6925-5ea3-925d-e697a6222064"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-40921"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-41919"] :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ 5{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear equations shown above. If the general least-squares solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $30a+\\frac{b}{c}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write our system in matrix form as $Ax=b,$ where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 5 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the corresponding normal equation:\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}\\,Ax={A}^{T}b\n$$\n\nNotice that the columns of $A$ are linearly dependent. So first, let's write down the normal equation in matrix form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -5 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 5 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -5 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}30 & -30 \\\\ -30 & 30\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system corresponding to the final matrix equation using Gaussian elimination, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}30 & -30 & 1 \\\\ -30 & 30 & -1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}30 & -30 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we have \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\frac{1}{30}+{x}_{2}.\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{30}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{30} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n30a+\\frac{b}{c}=30\\cdot \\frac{1}{30}+\\frac{1}{1}=2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-137096/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "b55251a9-c931-5eb6-baf8-3966a28e2642" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-137096/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "24f5c83d-7742-549e-be99-81aef55cc29e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-137096/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "44630438-796f-528e-9dc5-cd29f6652f8a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-137096/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "a169034c-2bd9-55d8-ac40-25818b93c57f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-137096/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "a0d94d77-a9af-562b-ba06-cc2e45c6044c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-137096/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e7f8a06e-80d1-5b8b-a269-2db2dc661081" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-137096/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-137096/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" "q-137096/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-137096/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-137096/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-137096/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-137096" :question/id #uuid "85757ebe-6f7f-5aa8-9cf4-901c45e3eda8" :question/math-academy-id "q-137096" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}=6 \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear equations shown above. If the general least-squares solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a-\\frac{3b}{c}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write our system in matrix form as $Ax=b,$ where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the corresponding normal equation:\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}\\,Ax={A}^{T}b\n$$\n\nNotice that the columns of $A$ are linearly dependent. So first, let's write down the normal equation in matrix form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}9 & 18 \\\\ 18 & 36\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ -18\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system corresponding to the final matrix equation using Gaussian elimination, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & 18 & -9 \\\\ 18 & 36 & -18\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}9 & 18 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we have \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=-1-2{x}_{2}.\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-1-2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na-\\frac{3b}{c}=-1-\\frac{3(-2)}{1}=5.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-137096/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8bc1e31e-5794-5ae3-8620-6bcaadde6a15"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-137096"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-137061/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "c0d53099-f8df-53c9-b5b9-81f2c39376a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-137061/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "65fe1574-7033-5bc7-a434-ec17d86082cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-137061/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "b9f5890d-287e-559b-a09f-bdb23c7df160" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-137061/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "ccf2cd19-f992-55fd-bcfb-b7e3d5e090c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-137061/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "bdecd056-0de1-55de-b344-ad53dfbb81d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-137061/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d7c75a6e-e41a-5989-94e6-598bbbf5adae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-137061/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-137061/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-137061/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-137061/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-137061/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-137061/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-137061" :question/id #uuid "ac571b42-2983-530f-a451-ee231a94a9ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-137061" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ {x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ -5{x}_{1}+10{x}_{2}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear equations shown above. If the general least-squares solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $2a+\\frac{b}{c}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write our system in matrix form as $Ax=b,$ where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -2 \\\\ -5 & 10\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the corresponding normal equation:\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}\\,Ax={A}^{T}b\n$$\n\nNotice that the columns of $A$ are linearly dependent. So first, let's write down the normal equation in matrix form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -5 \\\\ -4 & -2 & 10\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -2 \\\\ -5 & 10\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -5 \\\\ -4 & -2 & 10\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}30 & -60 \\\\ -60 & 120\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-15 \\\\ 30\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system corresponding to the above matrix equation using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -2 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we have \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=-\\frac{1}{2}+2{x}_{2}.\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2}+2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n2a+\\frac{b}{c}=2\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})+\\frac{2}{1}=1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-137061/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8bc1e31e-5794-5ae3-8620-6bcaadde6a15"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-137061"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-137119/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "2346a291-928a-5965-a144-7ecc1ea32e06" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-137119/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "ed082553-0997-5289-9588-a01c997c26a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-137119/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "b0198586-398c-5fe4-abeb-c098826a5744" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-137119/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "d44359c3-00f3-50d6-a486-c6b901c5a662" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-137119/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "d6a2e42c-ac8c-5a09-a4b5-31575b584f90" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-137119/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "06fb5ca0-97cf-599d-9d3f-54d5bb3dd03e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-137119/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-137119/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-137119/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-137119/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-137119/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-137119/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-137119" :question/id #uuid "7e13f62f-4b2e-5e53-998a-b4040c277b68" :question/math-academy-id "q-137119" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}=-2 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-6{x}_{2}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear equations shown above. If the general least-squares solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $7a+\\frac{b}{c}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write our system in matrix form as $Ax=b,$ where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -4 \\\\ 3 & -6\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the corresponding normal equation:\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}\\,Ax={A}^{T}b\n$$\n\nNotice that the columns of $A$ are linearly dependent. So first, let's write down the normal equation in matrix form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -4 & -6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -4 \\\\ 3 & -6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -4 & -6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}14 & -28 \\\\ -28 & 56\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system corresponding to the final matrix equation using Gaussian elimination, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}14 & -28 & -4 \\\\ -28 & 56 & 8\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}14 & -28 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we have \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=-\\frac{2}{7}+2{x}_{2}.\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{7}+2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{7} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n7a+\\frac{b}{c}=7\\cdot (-\\frac{2}{7})+\\frac{2}{1}=0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-137119/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8bc1e31e-5794-5ae3-8620-6bcaadde6a15"] :knowledge-point/ques